WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.025
Meta launched Muse Wonder and Full on October twelfth.

2
00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:11.695
Active Memory and Active Focus are Meta’s names for
their agent capabilities.

3
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.198
The API preview uses muse-wonder-1.0.

4
00:00:15.298 --> 00:00:18.173
Full requires an eligible Muse Code subscription.

5
00:00:18.273 --> 00:00:21.702
Maximum reasoning effort does not turn the API model
into Full.

6
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:28.493
MemoryBench tests recall from supplied conversations
of sixty-four to one hundred thousand tokens.

7
00:00:28.593 --> 00:00:32.641
That does not establish durable storage or retrieval
after a restart.

8
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.311
The methods matter.

9
00:00:34.411 --> 00:00:38.063
SWE-Marathon results use different agent products.

10
00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:42.669
That comparison combines model and harness effects; it
does not isolate the model.

11
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:50.220
On October fourteenth, Artificial Analysis lists
intelligence scores of fifty-two for Wonder and
fifty-six for Full, at maximum effort.

12
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.515
That composite does not measure your repository’s
reliability.

13
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.709
Compare complete systems: the model, tools,
permissions, and runtime.

14
00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:01.087
Then assess verified outcomes, elapsed time, and total
cost.

